PEG parsing based on the Lua lpeg machine described
by Ierusalimschy: https://www.inf.puc-rio.br/~roberto/docs/peg.pdf

The grammar source format is that of chpeg, https://github.com/ChrisHixon/chpeg/blob/master/grammars/chpeg.chpeg,
with the addition that a definition identifier starting with underscore
is not added to the parse tree, and definition options other than "I" are
ignored. Left-recursive definitions are detected but not handled.

Speed is competitive with cpp-peglib on a C lexical scanner for a large source file:
    chpeg time 0.044929792 seconds
    peglib time 0.027779792 seconds -38.2 %
    text 455620 end 455620 nodes 55419
    PEMachine time 0.02587575 seconds -42.4 %
Key speed gains are from:
    - decoding the subject string to an array of UTF16 code units,
    - using the function call stack to save state for match failure,
    - using a sequential tree structure,
    - not removing tails of varying size array structures.
A version of the machine using UnsafePointer gains even more:
    text 455620 end 455620 nodes 55419
    pointer machine time 0.019532209 seconds -56.5 %
An alternate implementation using class functions does not exceed:
    text 455620 end 455620 nodes 55419
    PEParser time 0.027070666 seconds -39.7 %
A third implementation using closures also does not exceed:
    text 455620 end 455620 nodes 55419
    PEGFun time 0.028257542 seconds -37.1 %
